--TEST--
A method called on a plain `object` or on a shape is `E0477` where it is written, never a panic below it — `rule:types/grammar`, `rule:types/erased-member-access`
--FILE--
<?nvs
final class Point {
    public int $x = 1;
    public function scaled(int $by): int {
        return $this->x * $by;
    }
}

// `rule:types/erased-member-access` gave the *property* half of an erased receiver a name-keyed
// runtime fetch and stopped there: a call additionally needs a signature to
// check its arguments against and a return type for the position it sits in,
// and `object` — `rule:types/grammar`'s opaque top of every class type — supplies
// neither. There is no `__call` to fall back on (`rule:classes/property-observer`).
object $o = new Point();
echo $o->scaled(3) as string, "\n";

// A shape is the structural type beside it, and `rule:types/object-top` gives it fields and
// no methods at all, so the same refusal covers it.
var $s = ({x: 1});
echo $s->scaled(3) as string, "\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0477]: `object` names no class, so it has no method `scaled`
   --> %s:15:6
   |
15 | echo $o->scaled(3) as string, "\n";
   |      ^^^^^^^^^^ called on a receiver that names no class here
   = help: narrow the receiver to the class that declares `scaled` first — `if ($x is ClassName) { … }`, or `$x as ClassName`; `rule:types/grammar` makes `object` the opaque top of every class type, and `rule:types/erased-member-access` erases a property access through one but not a call

error[E0477]: `{x: int}` names no class, so it has no method `scaled`
   --> %s:20:6
   |
20 | echo $s->scaled(3) as string, "\n";
   |      ^^^^^^^^^^ called on a receiver that names no class here
   = help: narrow the receiver to the class that declares `scaled` first — `if ($x is ClassName) { … }`, or `$x as ClassName`; `rule:types/grammar` makes `object` the opaque top of every class type, and `rule:types/erased-member-access` erases a property access through one but not a call

